{"type": "message", "id": "5a967b4a", "parentId": "d7a03be8", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:17:49.834Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I now have all the data I need. Let me summarize:\n\n**FRED Median Listing Prices for January 2023:**\n- Kentucky: $281,261 (between $280k-$300k ✓)\n- Arizona: $461,700 (above $300k ✗)\n- South Carolina: $349,900 (above $300k ✗)\n- Kansas: $285,570 (between $280k-$300k ✓)\n\n**NAEP 2022 Grade 8 Math Scores:**\n- Kentucky: 270 (from the search results showing \"272 for the Nation and 270 for Kentucky\")\n- Arizona: Need to verify\n- South Carolina: 269 (from search results)\n- Kansas: 272 or 274 (from search results, both above 270 ✓)\n\nNow I need to find the NAEP scores for Arizona and confirm Kentucky's score."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "functions.web_search:56", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 math Arizona average score", "count": 10}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "functions.web_search:57", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 math Kentucky average score 270", "count": 10}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "modelstudio", "model": "kimi-k2.5", "usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 0, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775301450875, "responseId": "chatcmpl-37c90ea6-aae3-9ddc-9dcd-ff5e6245190d"}}
{"type": "message", "id": "6829159f", "parentId": "5a967b4a", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:17:50.820Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:56", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"NAEP 2022 grade 8 math Arizona average score\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 983,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d48932345e2d7b8b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d48932345e2d7b8b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"77920fdbe7ff8561\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from <strong>2 to 14 points</strong>. The average score decline for public schools in the nation decreased by 5 points. To view score changes for fourth-grade public school students in mathematics ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"77920fdbe7ff8561\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"75c5516cf4b65784\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ARIZONA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"75c5516cf4b65784\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011AZ8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e53125433128b127\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: Puerto Rico was not included in the comparison results. AVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBLIC) ... White students. This performance gap was not significantly different from that in 2000 ... NOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e53125433128b127\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57b23c2c3f85739f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57b23c2c3f85739f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"05fb3bef7a9e1825\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics ... compared to 2019. Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from <strong>0 to 500</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"05fb3bef7a9e1825\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"83d739836d9a5bbf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"83d739836d9a5bbf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"822cafe11eac5fea\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nlevel was <strong>60 percent</strong> in 2022. This percentage was smaller than that in 2019 (68 · percent) and was not significantly different from that in 2000 (62 percent). NAEP ACHIEVEMENT-LEVEL PERCENTAGES AND AVERAGE SCORE\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"822cafe11eac5fea\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a60d3e85745cc00\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP | Arizona Department of Education\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a60d3e85745cc00\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.azed.gov/assessment/naep\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"70ec09e3c836426e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nnaep-logo.jpg The National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) is the largest nationally continuing evaluation of the condition of education in the United States. NAEP has served as a national yardstick of student achievement since 1969.Through The Nation’s Report Card, NAEP informs the public what American students know in various subject areas and compares achievement among states, large urban districts, and various student groups.NAEP is a congressionally mandated program administered by the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) within the U.S.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"70ec09e3c836426e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 14, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.azed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"97c51896d326d21d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAverage National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) mathematics scale score of 8th-grade public school students, by race/ethnicity, parents' highest level of education, and state or jurisdiction: 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"97c51896d326d21d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/programs/digest/d23/tables/dt23_222.70.asp\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef440453ee067afb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPrevious Page Download Excel (38KB)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef440453ee067afb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d9837311833d7ff9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d9837311833d7ff9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a6e143ad980ea67\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUse the drop-down menu to select a state/jurisdiction and click on a student group thumbnail to see average mathematics scores for fourth-grade public school students over time in the selected state/jurisdiction. ... Use the drop-down menus to select a state/jurisdiction and a student group to view changes in the percentage distribution for that group over time. Read about changes in NAEP&#x27;s reporting for racial/ethnic groups.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a6e143ad980ea67\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fcb094ac96d5d5fe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fcb094ac96d5d5fe\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1f7ccbc5dced8903\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAverage Scale Scores: 2022............................................................................... <strong>19 ...</strong> of structural prompts such as diagrams, charts, and graphs. They should be able to solve problems in · all NAEP content areas through the appropriate selection and use of strategies ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1f7ccbc5dced8903\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.fldoe.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7677a41c4a22374d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe New NAEP Scores Highlight a Standards Gap in Many States - FutureEd\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7677a41c4a22374d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.future-ed.org/the-new-naep-scores-highlight-a-standards-gap-in-many-states/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fb93d306d474b7a5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nForty-seven states improved NAEP math proficiency rates between 2022 and 2024 in fourth grade and 36 states did so in eighth grade. But proficiency rates remain below 2019 levels in 34 states in fourth-grade and in all but one state in eighth-grade. Similarly, math proficiency rates rose on nearly every state’s standardized tests during the same period. While state math scores declined dramatically between 2019 and 2022, particularly in eighth grade, only in Arizona, Arkansas, Florida, Idaho, and Vermont in fourth grade and Arkansas, Michigan, and Missouri in eighth grade did state test scores decline between 2022 and 2024.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fb93d306d474b7a5\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.future-ed.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6eda7baccfae9506\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: National Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6eda7baccfae9506\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/nation/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"badab132a1cab632\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP reports scores at five selected percentiles to show the progress made by lower- (10th and 25th percentiles), middle- (50th percentile), and higher- (75th and 90th percentiles) performing students. In comparison to 2019, the 2022 mathematics scores were lower for fourth-grade students at all five selected percentiles.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"badab132a1cab632\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 math Arizona average score", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 983, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d48932345e2d7b8b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d48932345e2d7b8b\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"77920fdbe7ff8561\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from <strong>2 to 14 points</strong>. The average score decline for public schools in the nation decreased by 5 points. To view score changes for fourth-grade public school students in mathematics ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"77920fdbe7ff8561\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"75c5516cf4b65784\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ARIZONA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"75c5516cf4b65784\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011AZ8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e53125433128b127\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: Puerto Rico was not included in the comparison results. AVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBLIC) ... White students. This performance gap was not significantly different from that in 2000 ... NOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e53125433128b127\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57b23c2c3f85739f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57b23c2c3f85739f\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"05fb3bef7a9e1825\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics ... compared to 2019. Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from <strong>0 to 500</strong>....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"05fb3bef7a9e1825\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"83d739836d9a5bbf\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"83d739836d9a5bbf\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"822cafe11eac5fea\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nlevel was <strong>60 percent</strong> in 2022. This percentage was smaller than that in 2019 (68 · percent) and was not significantly different from that in 2000 (62 percent). NAEP ACHIEVEMENT-LEVEL PERCENTAGES AND AVERAGE SCORE\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"822cafe11eac5fea\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2a60d3e85745cc00\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP | Arizona Department of Education\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2a60d3e85745cc00\">>>", "url": "https://www.azed.gov/assessment/naep", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"70ec09e3c836426e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nnaep-logo.jpg The National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) is the largest nationally continuing evaluation of the condition of education in the United States. NAEP has served as a national yardstick of student achievement since 1969.Through The Nation’s Report Card, NAEP informs the public what American students know in various subject areas and compares achievement among states, large urban districts, and various student groups.NAEP is a congressionally mandated program administered by the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) within the U.S.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"70ec09e3c836426e\">>>", "published": "July 14, 2025", "siteName": "www.azed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"97c51896d326d21d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAverage National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) mathematics scale score of 8th-grade public school students, by race/ethnicity, parents' highest level of education, and state or jurisdiction: 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"97c51896d326d21d\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/programs/digest/d23/tables/dt23_222.70.asp", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ef440453ee067afb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nPrevious Page Download Excel (38KB)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ef440453ee067afb\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d9837311833d7ff9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d9837311833d7ff9\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a6e143ad980ea67\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nUse the drop-down menu to select a state/jurisdiction and click on a student group thumbnail to see average mathematics scores for fourth-grade public school students over time in the selected state/jurisdiction. ... Use the drop-down menus to select a state/jurisdiction and a student group to view changes in the percentage distribution for that group over time. Read about changes in NAEP&#x27;s reporting for racial/ethnic groups.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a6e143ad980ea67\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fcb094ac96d5d5fe\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_