{"type": "message", "id": "dfd9deb0", "parentId": "480318d2", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:18:16.505Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:65", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"\\\"Kansas\\\" \\\"2022\\\" \\\"NAEP\\\" \\\"grade 8\\\" \\\"math\\\" \\\"average score\\\" \\\"272\\\" OR \\\"273\\\" OR \\\"274\\\"\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 869,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c715f3dcb0388841\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KANSAS  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c715f3dcb0388841\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KS8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be108767f1c2910d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP · Advanced · level · In · 2022 · = 5 · In · 2019 · = 9, significantly · different · from · the · state&#x27;s · results · in · 2022. In · 2000 · = 5 · Average · score · in · the · Nation · in · 2022 · = 273. Average · score · in · Kansas · In · 2022 · = 272 ·\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be108767f1c2910d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3e881ea367edd4bf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n72% of Kansas 8th Graders Aren’t Proficient in Math | Aligned\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3e881ea367edd4bf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.wearealigned.org/blogs/72-kansas-8th-graders-arent-proficient-math\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6b6df1c20059a18\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAccording to the 2022 NAEP (Nation’s Report Card): 72% of Kansas 8th graders are below proficient in math. Kansas’s average 8th-grade score: 274, which is <strong>slightly above the national average, but far from top-performing states</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6b6df1c20059a18\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 1, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.wearealigned.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db0aaf9be160a7a5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db0aaf9be160a7a5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"84a304c79d8e31f8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP Mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Observed differences are not necessarily statistically significant. Basic · Proficient · Advanced · Page 10 · 266 · 275 · 282 283 · 288 288 · 280 · 287 · 272 · 268 · 273 275 · 281 281 279 282 · 277 · 268 · 274 277 ·\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"84a304c79d8e31f8\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.fldoe.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a4912f07c3c259eb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAnalysis of 2022 NAEP Mathematics and Reading Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a4912f07c3c259eb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://whiteboardadvisors.com/analysis-of-2022-naep-mathematics-and-reading-results/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e3e477cf093679b2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAverage eighth grade scores were lower than all previous assessment years dating to 1998 — and not significantly higher than scores in 1992. <strong>Average eighth grade math score fell from 282 in 2019 to 274 in 2022</strong> – a decline of 8 points\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e3e477cf093679b2\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 24, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"whiteboardadvisors.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15d5197593183c25\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOVEMBER 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15d5197593183c25\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"103b9ceec96c8b1e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nProcess (NAEP). 2022 Mathematics Assessment. The decline in mathematics scores in the eighth grade is more significant, as 10 states fell below the national average · (274). Virginia (279) was the only state to score above the national average. Missouri (272), North Carolina (274), Tennessee (272), and Texas (273...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"103b9ceec96c8b1e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"csgsouth.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b56842d0055bf238\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUnderstanding Results of State Tests in the Context of the National Assessment: A Look at Grade 8 Mathematics in Kansas and Iowa\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b56842d0055bf238\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://danmcgrath2.substack.com/p/understanding-results-of-state-tests\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"edc6dda3a1be3328\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIf you put their threshold for proficient on the NAEP scale in 2022 it would sit at about <strong>302 points</strong>, which is a bit higher than NAEP’s own NAEP Proficient threshold (299 points).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"edc6dda3a1be3328\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 28, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"danmcgrath2.substack.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4d59243626b5ff1c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search