and Iowa\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b56842d0055bf238\">>>", "url": "https://danmcgrath2.substack.com/p/understanding-results-of-state-tests", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"edc6dda3a1be3328\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIf you put their threshold for proficient on the NAEP scale in 2022 it would sit at about <strong>302 points</strong>, which is a bit higher than NAEP’s own NAEP Proficient threshold (299 points).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"edc6dda3a1be3328\">>>", "published": "January 28, 2026", "siteName": "danmcgrath2.substack.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4d59243626b5ff1c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ALASKA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4d59243626b5ff1c\">>>", "url": "https://education.alaska.gov/assessments/snapshot_MAT2022AK_8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"41288ca9db5f1b62\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<strong>lower than the average score of 273 for students in the nation</strong>. ... * Significantly different (p &lt; .05) from state&#x27;s results in 2022. Significance tests were performed using ... NOTE: Puerto Rico was not included in the comparison results. AVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"41288ca9db5f1b62\">>>", "siteName": "education.alaska.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c5a88893d601f792\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c5a88893d601f792\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2d185079196a9091\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2d185079196a9091\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2e9453354f512b1f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nStates’ Demographically Adjusted Performance on the 2022 Nation’s Report Card\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2e9453354f512b1f\">>>", "url": "https://www.urban.org/sites/default/files/2024-12/States_Demographically_Adjusted_Performance_on_the_2022_Nations_Report_Card.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3a2fe355e5404efb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n272.9 · 264.2 · 259.3 · Oklahoma · 239.9 · 232.2 · 219.6 · 212.4 · 279.0 · 267.1 · 260.8 · 253.8 · Oregon · 232.0 · 220.6 · 212.8 · 202.7 · 275.4 · 262.6 · 260.4 · 251.2 · Pennsylvania · 240.9 · 234.7 · 220.5 · 216.0 · 282.7 · 271.3 · 262.2 · 257.2 · Rhode Island · 238.0 · 232.5 · 218.1 · 215.6 · 274.6 · 268.8 · 261.0 · 258.1 · South Carolina · 240.2 · 238.0 · 219.2 · 220.4 · 281.4 · 273.7 ·\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3a2fe355e5404efb\">>>", "siteName": "www.urban.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cd0339af7edd9d07\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT MISSOURI  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cd0339af7edd9d07\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011MO8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"982c8a5a6570eb68\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP · Advanced · level · In · 2022 · = 5 · In · 2019 · = 7, significantly · different · from · the · state&#x27;s · results · in · 2022. In · 2000 · = 2, significantly · different · from · the · state&#x27;s · results · in · 2022. Average · score · in · the · Nation · in · 2022 · = 273. Average · score · in · Missouri · In · 2022 · = 272 ·\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"982c8a5a6570eb68\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775301496497}}
